Date: Tue, 5 Feb 2019 06:30:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] udevadm info: "-a" should enumerate sysfs attributes, not
 envs (#11642)

This fixes a bug introduced by 13aca847695f49afeb93367ecdad76035fa6c139.

diff --git a/src/udev/udevadm-info.c b/src/udev/udevadm-info.c
index 135a5e0120..ebd15d384a 100644
--- a/src/udev/udevadm-info.c
+++ b/src/udev/udevadm-info.c
@@ -61,12 +61,15 @@ static bool skip_attribute(const char *name) {
 static void print_all_attributes(sd_device *device, const char *key) {
         const char *name, *value;

-        FOREACH_DEVICE_PROPERTY(device, name, value) {
+        FOREACH_DEVICE_SYSATTR(device, name) {
                 size_t len;

                 if (skip_attribute(name))
                         continue;

+                if (sd_device_get_sysattr_value(device, name, &value) < 0)
+                        continue;
+
                 /* skip any values that look like a path */
                 if (value[0] == '/')
                         continue;
-- 
2.25.1

        You will be given the root cause of a bug, the commit message and the corresponding patch.
        You need to extract all code statements that lead to the bug from the patch, based on the root cause and the commit message.

        Root cause:
        The bug was caused by the use of `FOREACH_DEVICE_PROPERTY` to enumerate device properties instead of using `FOREACH_DEVICE_SYSATTR` to enumerate sysfs attributes. This led to the incorrect behavior of the `-a` option in `udevadm info`, which was supposed to list sysfs attributes but instead listed environment properties.

        Commit message:
        udevadm info: "-a" should enumerate sysfs attributes, not
 envs (#11642)

This fixes a bug introduced by 13aca847695f49afeb93367ecdad76035fa6c139.  

        Patch:

 static void print_all_attributes(sd_device *device, const char *key) {
         const char *name, *value;

-        FOREACH_DEVICE_PROPERTY(device, name, value) {
+        FOREACH_DEVICE_SYSATTR(device, name) {
                 size_t len;

                 if (skip_attribute(name))
                         continue;

+                if (sd_device_get_sysattr_value(device, name, &value) < 0)
+                        continue;
+
                 /* skip any values that look like a path */
                 if (value[0] == '/')
                         continue;

                 /* skip nonprintable attributes */
                 len = strlen(value);
                 while (len > 0 && isprint(value[len-1]))
                         len--;
                 if (len > 0)
                         continue;

                 printf("    %s{%s}==\"%s\"\n", key, name, value);
         }
         puts("");
 }



